# Cached API responses — regenerated by `scripts/batch_fetch.py`. We use
# `cache/*` (not `cache/`) so that single-file negations below actually
# work — git ignores ALL files in a directory once the directory itself
# is excluded, even with a later "!" rule. With `cache/*` the directory
# isn't excluded, only its contents are, so the manifest negation lands.
cache/*
# EXCEPT the wiki icon manifest — that's the per-item-id image override
# table built by scripts/scrape_wiki_icons.py, consumed by
# build_page_data.py to map items_assets to assets/items_wiki/ paths.
# Without this file present, build_page_data falls through to the
# deadlock-api icon namespace (assets/items/) where 60 items collide
# on shared filenames and unrelated items wear each other's icons.
!cache/wiki_icon_overrides.json
# ... and the match-only archetype resolutions. resolve-archetypes.yml
# has always tried to commit these ("git add -A cache/match_archetype_resolutions/")
# but this ignore file silently blocked it, so every resolution lived only
# in the Actions cache — and died with the v1→v2 cache-key bump. Tracking
# them makes each (patch, hero, fingerprint) resolution a one-time cost.
!cache/match_archetype_resolutions/

# Validation harness outputs (regenerated by `validation/harness.py`)
validation/window_cache/
validation/reports/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code worktree state
.claude/
